{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They are transported</b> — Some say: and they did not transport from them, and the meaning is that they did not speak until a person would transport their words. Or its interpretation may be: they are transported, from עתק, that the words have transported from them."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The root עתק (ʿ-t-q) carries the sense of removal/transfer; the comment turns on whether the verb is active or passive and whether the subject is the men or their words."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:15.873740627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}